today I'm going to show you one of  Mexico's most popular cocktails and no  it's not the margarita it is the lesser  known and perilously refreshing Paloma  for this cocktail you're going to need  some Blanco tequila a couple lime wedges  a pinch of salt and some grapefruit soda  we're going to start by building this  right in the glass kind of the way you  would a gin and tonic or a rum and coke  so we're going to start with two ounces  of Blanco tequila there are three major  kinds of tequila Blanco Reposado and  Anejo  Blanco means white and it's barely been  aged at all the Reposado means rested  means it's been aged for up to a year  has a slightly yellow ER color and then  an yaho means aged and has spent about  one to three years in a barrel it's more  complex and has more of an amber color  but for mixing really refreshing  cocktails like this or a margarita  Blanco is the best way to go all right  so we're gonna fill this glass with ice  threw in a pinch of salt right over the  top you'll see some recipes that call  for a salt rim I just like to throw it  right in and now a lime wedge which  we're going to squeeze over the ice and  just toss it in and now we're ready for  our grapefruit soda there are not that  many grapefruit soda brands around in  the US market there's some really good  mexican brands out there if you can find  those but if you can't find any you can  also substitute some grapefruit juice  agave and soda water so just do an ounce  of grapefruit juice half an ounce of  agave nectar and top it with soda stir  it up finally finish it off with the  language that is the Paloma your summer  alternative to the margarita what's your  favorite drink tell us in the comments  below  you
 

